<title>UK: Natural rubber stocks continue to fall in May.</title>
<headline>Natural rubber stocks continue to fall in May.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>World natural rubber stocks fell for the fourth successive month in May 1996 by 80,000 tonnes from the previous month, according to latest data from the International Rubber Study Group.</p>
<p>    Data in thousand tonnes  --  MAY'96     APR'96     MAY'95</p>
<p>    Natural production		  420	  410	  430</p>
<p>    Natural consumption		 500	  500	  500</p>
<p>    Natural stocks		    1,470	1,550	1,540</p>
<p>    Synthetic production		800	  820	  850</p>
<p>    Synthetic consumption	     810	  790	  800</p>
<p>    Synthetic stocks		  2,060	2,070	1,980</p>
<p>London Newsroom +44 171 542 7771</p>
